<Magazine title="A magazine for our people"><section class="about-page wrap"><span class="eyebrow">HELLO, GOOD COMPANY.</span><h1>Your friends.<br /><em>Front-page material.</em></h1><div class="about-body"><div class="prose"><p>We think our friends deserve the magazine treatment.</p><p>A first film credit. A project finally out in the world. A small, wildly interesting thing that happened on a Tuesday. Vanity Vair is a place to give those stories a little room.</p><h2>The group chat has a front page.</h2><p>We’re a small, independent publication rooted in Vancouver, made by friends, for friends, and for anyone curious enough to stop by. Write something, make something, tell us what’s new.</p><h2 id="promotions">And yes, the “ads” are our friends, too.</h2><p>The promotions you see here are handpicked businesses and projects from our circle. Think of them as very enthusiastic introductions.</p><p><strong>Every promotion is free.</strong> No money changes hands for a feature or an ad. Vanity Vair is free to read and contribute to, and we don’t operate for profit. There’s no advertising network following you around.</p><h2>V is for Vancouver.</h2><p>Why the V instead of an F? Vancouver. Vanity Vair gives our city and the people in our circle the magazine treatment: the films, the projects, the milestones, and the everyday stories worth sharing. Big cover-star energy, close to home.</p><h2>A note on the name</h2><p>Vanity Vair is an independent parody publication. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Vanity Fair or Condé Nast.</p><p>Please visit the <a href="https://www.vanityfair.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official Vanity Fair website</a> and enjoy the articles created by its hardworking writers, editors, photographers, and contributors. Give their work some love, too.</p><p class="sample-disclosure">This preview contains fictional sample contributors, stories, and businesses, with illustrative photography from Unsplash. Real stories are coming.</p></div></div></section></Magazine>
